                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Almost two hours, and I completed the original Dead Pixels game. \n\nFor £1.99 it was worth it, simple as. With it's 2D graphical aesthetics, it's RPG elements in terms of levelling up your characters skills and perks, it was simple mechanic; kill the dead, loot the empty shops and premises for stuff to sell to a vendor. Buy ammunition, new weapons alongside the ones you discover yourself and rinse and repeat.\n\nA mechanic that can get grinding, or grating but not Dead Pixels. I completed the original game in one sitting, even when I got surrounded and killed I started from my last save point at a vendor's and tried again. Finding upgrading skills from running, to weapon damage and even luck alongside carrying capacity it was exciting. It can feel run and gun, but if you don't have the ammunition or the next level of the weapon you will struggle. Plus picking off the weaker, slower zombies before taking on the tougher, stronger enemies took some time to get used to. \n\nThe Solution and Last Stand modes have added even more value, in the Solution you pick a named survivor whom is a homage to characters from Zombie films and such, including someone named R KIRMAN which I think was a nod to the creator of The Walking Dead. In this mode, there are no shops to buy or sell wares to, supplies are ordered by a limited number of radio uses and dropped into you but still using cash taken from killing the undead. With even ink ribons as a homage to Resident Evil to save your progress.\n\nThe Last Stand adds more fun, holding off wave after wave of the undead in a mall with stores to buy what you need to survive. For what I paid and the consistent amount of fun I've enjoyed from it I am a satisfied customer. \n\nI am also looking forward to the sequel once it's released. \n\n10/10",
